{"1-8":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":5,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"deborah-h1683g","name":"Deborah","kind":"person","brief":"A nurse","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"rebekah-h7259","name":"Rebekah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Laban","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"places":[{"id":"bethel-h1008g","name":"Bethel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":5,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"shechem-h7927g","name":"Shechem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":4},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"allon-bacuth-h0439","name":"Allon-bacuth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"words":[{"base":"H1008","lemma":"בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל","tr":"bet-el","gloss":"Bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":142},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":350},{"base":"H0416","lemma":"אֵל בֵּית־אֵל","tr":"el bet-el","gloss":"El-bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":3},{"base":"H8033","lemma":"שָׁם","tr":"sham","gloss":"there","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":834},{"base":"H0439","lemma":"אַלּוֹן בָּכוּת","tr":"al·lon ba·khut","gloss":"Allon-bacuth","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H4196","lemma":"מִזְבֵּחַ","tr":"miz·be·ach","gloss":"altar","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":401},{"base":"H5236","lemma":"נֵכָר","tr":"ne·khar","gloss":"foreign","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":36},{"base":"H8478","lemma":"תַּחַת","tr":"ta·chat","gloss":"underneath: under","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":505},{"base":"H1272","lemma":"בָּרַח","tr":"ba·rach","gloss":"to flee","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":65},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1051}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":19,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"Then the LORD said to Moses, “Go to the people and consecrate them today and tomorrow. They must wash their clothes","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":19,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"When Moses came down from the mountain to the people, he consecrated them, and they washed their clothes.","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":31,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"I am the God of Bethel, where you anointed the pillar and made a solemn vow to Me. Now get up and leave this land at once, and return to your native land.’”","from":1},{"book":"EXO","chapter":23,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"I will send My terror ahead of you and throw into confusion every nation you encounter. I will make all your enemies turn and run.","from":5},{"book":"JAS","chapter":4,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Draw near to God, and He will draw near to you. Cleanse your hands, you sinners, and purify your hearts, you double-minded.","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":59,"verseEnd":59,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So they sent their sister Rebekah on her way, along with her nurse and Abrahamʼs servant and his men.","from":8},{"book":"2CH","chapter":17,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And the dread of the LORD fell upon all the kingdoms of the lands that surrounded Judah, so that they did not make war against Jehoshaphat.","from":5},{"book":"ISA","chapter":43,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"When you pass through the waters, I will be with you; and when you go through the rivers, they will not overwhelm you. When you walk through the fire, you will not be scorched; the flames will not set you ablaze.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"9-15":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":12}],"places":[{"id":"paddan-h6307","name":"Paddan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"bethel-h1008g","name":"Bethel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":15}],"words":[{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":350},{"base":"H8034","lemma":"שֵׁם","tr":"shem","gloss":"name","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":864},{"base":"H4725","lemma":"מָקוֹם","tr":"ma·qom","gloss":"place","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":401},{"base":"H7121","lemma":"קָרָא","tr":"qa·ra","gloss":"to call: call to","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":733},{"base":"H0854","lemma":"אֵת","tr":"et","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":929},{"base":"H1008","lemma":"בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל","tr":"bet-el","gloss":"Bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":142},{"base":"H1696","lemma":"דָבַר","tr":"da·var","gloss":"to speak: speak","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1142},{"base":"H5750","lemma":"עוֹד","tr":"od","gloss":"still","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":490},{"base":"H1471","lemma":"גּוֹי","tr":"goy","gloss":"nation","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":561},{"base":"H4678","lemma":"מַצֶּבֶת","tr":"mats·tse·vet","gloss":"pillar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"No longer will you be called Abram, but your name will be Abraham, for I have made you a father of many nations.","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"When Abram was ninety-nine years old, the Lordappeared to him and said, “I am God Almighty. Walk before Me and be blameless.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"“What is your name?” the man asked. “Jacob,” he replied.","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":32,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Then the man said, “Your name will no longer be Jacob, but Israel, because you have struggled with God and with men, and you have prevailed.”","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"And God blessed Noah and his sons and said to them, “Be fruitful and multiply and fill the earth.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lordappeared to Abram and said, “I will give this land to your offspring.” So Abram built an altar there to the Lord, who had appeared to him.","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then God said to Abraham, “As for Sarai your wife, do not call her Sarai, for her name is to be Sarah.","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":22,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I will surely bless you, and I will multiply your descendants like the stars in the sky and the sand on the seashore. Your descendants will possess the gates of their enemies.","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"16-20":{"people":[{"id":"rachel-h7354","name":"Rachel","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Leah","count":3,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":20}],"places":[{"id":"bethlehem-h1035g","name":"Bethlehem","kind":"place","brief":"In Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"bethel-h1008g","name":"Bethel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"words":[{"base":"H7354","lemma":"רָחֵל","tr":"ra·chel","gloss":"Rachel","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":47},{"base":"H1126","lemma":"בֶּן־אוֹנִ֑י","tr":"ben-o·ni","gloss":"Ben-oni","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":496},{"base":"H0672","lemma":"אֶפְרָ֫תָה","tr":"eph·ra·tah","gloss":"Ephrathah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H6900","lemma":"קְבֻרָה","tr":"qe·vu·rah","gloss":"tomb","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H7185","lemma":"קָשָׁה","tr":"qa·shah","gloss":"to harden","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":28},{"base":"H1035","lemma":"בֵּית לֶ֫חֶם","tr":"bet le·chem","gloss":"Bethlehem","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":82},{"base":"H1008","lemma":"בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל","tr":"bet-el","gloss":"Bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":142},{"base":"H3530","lemma":"כִּבְרָה","tr":"kiv·rah","gloss":"distance","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4678","lemma":"מַצֶּבֶת","tr":"mats·tse·vet","gloss":"pillar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":10,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"When you leave me today, you will find two men at Rachelʼs tomb in Zelzah on the border of Benjamin. They will say to you, ‘The donkeys you seek have been found, and now your father has stopped worrying about the donkeys and started worrying about you, asking, “What should I do about my son?”’","from":20},{"book":"MIC","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, who are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come forth for Me One to be ruler over Israel— One whose origins are of old, from the days of eternity.","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":30,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"She named him Joseph, and said, “May the Lordadd to me another son.”","from":17},{"book":"GEN","chapter":48,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now as for me, when I was returning from Paddan, to my sorrow Rachel died along the way in the land of Canaan, some distance from Ephrath. So I buried her there beside the road to Ephrath” (that is, Bethlehem).","from":19},{"book":"MIC","chapter":5,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, who are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come forth for Me One to be ruler over Israel— One whose origins are of old, from the days of eternity.","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":3,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"To the woman He said: “I will sharply increase your pain in childbirth; in pain you will bring forth children. Your desire will be for your husband, and he will rule over you.”","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":30,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Rachel saw that she was not bearing any children for Jacob, she envied her sister. “Give me children, or I will die!” she said to Jacob.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"After Jacob had returned from Paddan-aram, God appeared to him again and blessed him.","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"21-29":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":6,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"bilhah-h1090a","name":"Bilhah","kind":"person","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"leah-h3812","name":"Leah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Rachel","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"issachar-h3485g","name":"Issachar","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"simeon-h8095g","name":"Simeon","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"zebulun-h2074","name":"Zebulun","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"rachel-h7354","name":"Rachel","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Leah","count":2,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"dan-h1835h","name":"Dan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"naphtali-h5321g","name":"Naphtali","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"asher-h0836","name":"Asher","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"gad-h1410g","name":"Gad","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"zilpah-h2153","name":"Zilpah","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":3,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"places":[{"id":"tower-of-eder-h4029","name":"Tower of Eder","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"paddan-h6307","name":"Paddan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"mamre-h4471g","name":"Mamre","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"words":[{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":350},{"base":"H3327","lemma":"יִצְחָק","tr":"yits·chaq","gloss":"Isaac","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":108},{"base":"H4029","lemma":"מִגְדַּל־עֵ֫דֶר","tr":"mig·dal-e·der","gloss":"tower of Eder","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H1090","lemma":"בִּלְהָה","tr":"bil·hah","gloss":"Bilhah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H7153","lemma":"קִרְיַת אַרְבַּע","tr":"qir·yat ar·ba","gloss":"Kiriath-arba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H3812","lemma":"לֵאָה","tr":"le·ah","gloss":"Leah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":34},{"base":"H7354","lemma":"רָחֵל","tr":"ra·chel","gloss":"Rachel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":47},{"base":"H8198","lemma":"שִׁפְחָה","tr":"shiph·chah","gloss":"maidservant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":63},{"base":"H7205","lemma":"רְאוּבֵן","tr":"re·u·ven","gloss":"Reuben","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":72},{"base":"H2153","lemma":"זִלְפָּה","tr":"zil·pah","gloss":"Zilpah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"These were the sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel. Though he was the firstborn, his birthright was given to the sons of Joseph son of Israel, because Reuben defiled his fatherʼs bed. So he is not reckoned according to birthright.","from":22},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"You, however, will go to your fathers in peace and be buried at a ripe old age.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So Abram moved his tent and went to live near the Oaks of Mamre at Hebron, where he built an altar to the Lord.","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Abraham lived a total of 175 years.","from":28},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"When Jacob had finished instructing his sons, he pulled his feet into the bed and breathed his last, and he was gathered to his people.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":23,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"After this, Abraham buried his wife Sarah in the cave of the field at Machpelah near Mamre (that is, Hebron) in the land of Canaan.","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"There Abraham and his wife Sarah are buried, there Isaac and his wife Rebekah are buried, and there I buried Leah.","from":29},{"book":"GEN","chapter":50,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So Joseph died at the age of 110. And they embalmed his body and placed it in a coffin in Egypt.","from":28}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":20}]}}